ir-code-induced-balance-entropy-nogo.statement:
For every deterministic length-n private-message code on a finite-alphabet memoryless broadcast channel, with independent uniform messages A,B, decoder errors p1,p2, Fano quantities Fj=h2(pj)+pj log2(Nj-1), and Si=(Y^{i-1},Z_{i+1}^n), the exact telescope
sum_i [I(A;B|Si,Yi)-I(A;B|Si,Zi)] = I(A;B|Y^n)-I(A;B|Z^n)
implies, after independent uniform time sharing T and setting U=A, V=B, W=S_T, X=X_T, that
|I(U;V|W,T,Y)-I(U;V|W,T,Z)| <= max(F1/n,F2/n).
The induced law preserves U independent of V, T independent of (U,V), the fixed coordinate encoder X=f_T(U,V), the condition that W cannot select a different map after (U,V,T) are fixed, and four compatible individual- and sum-rate rows:
R1 <= I(U,W;Y|T)+F1/n;
R2 <= I(V,W;Z|T)+F2/n;
R1+R2 <= I(U,W;Y|T)+I(X;Z|U,W,T)+(F1+F2)/n;
R1+R2 <= I(V,W;Z|T)+I(X;Y|V,W,T)+(F1+F2)/n.
At uniform BSSC input, the associated coarse relaxation imposing the complete seven entropies of the common-noise coupling, the code-structural equalities, exact dependence balance, every stated conditional BEC identity, and the two sharp scalar posterior-support inequalities has an actual finite entropic witness for which both direct sum branches equal 2h2(1/4)-5/4 = 0.3725562489182657.... Therefore no collection of universally valid finite-variable information inequalities, and no finite sequence of standard copy-lemma extensions, can lower that relaxation below this value.
